        "problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix.",
        "worked_solution": "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z=2 \\\\ 0x+y-3z=1 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=-3,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution.",
