        "problem": "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $P,$ given by\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]?\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & ↔{R}_{4} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $4$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th columns.",
